What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only diagnostic snapshot of the MT6580 PCM suspend provider.
		mode=load-only identifies the initial instruction-fetch stage;
		mode=retained-run executes PCM with retention flags and clock/memory
		requests held by default. R7 is connected for timer/control sequencing;
		R0 defaults to disconnected, with optional qualification below.
		pcm_words and dma identify the coherent instruction buffer. loads
		counts completed instruction fetches, not PCM sleep executions.
		last_error is the last loader/handoff errno; loaded_fsm and
		restored_fsm record its hardware FSM values. fsm/con0/con1/pwr_io
		are live always-on SPM registers. No write operation is provided.
		runs counts execution attempts, irqs counts normal IRQ handler
		dispatches, and pending records the GIC pending state at cleanup.
		Normal suspend return is acknowledged in the atomic entry callback,
		so irqs may remain zero despite a real SPM timer wake. forced_exit
		means CPU_WAKE was requested after an external IRQ returned WFI.
		wake fields contain PCM R11/R12/R13, raw/misc/timer, return ISR,
		event, PC, assertion and debug snapshots. power/power2 compare the
		two power-status registers before and after the retained run.
		timer_cfg/val/at_wake record timer setup and its state immediately
		after WFI, before any forced PCM exit. wake_pwr_io/flags/src_req
		record the applied R7 connection and retention constraints.
		source before/applied record the original and selected SRC_REQ;
		CCIF event masks are preserved, APSRC bit 0 defaults to asserted, and
		software F26M bit 1 is omitted only if all configured UARTs completed
		their sleep handshake, USB PHY/clocks are shut down and DISP/MFG
		are off. blockers bits retain
		F26M for an unready UART (0), powered DISP/MFG (1), an unqualified
		POWER_ON_VAL0/1 baseline (2), or an existing firmware F26M request
		(3), or USB PHY/clocks not shut down (4). usb_ready is a bit mask
		of configured USB controllers with completed late-suspend handoff.
		Source snapshots also include pre-run R13, POWER_ON_VAL0/1,
		CLK_CON, AP_STANDBY and MMDDR_MASK. These show request ownership;
		they do not establish that 26 MHz physically stopped. r0_control
		and apsrc_control explicitly override their respective defaults.
		f26m_control additionally releases the F26M override with all guards.
		cpu0 mode/resumes/result record CPU0 resume-entry qualification.
		vector contains the original/programmed/restored shared boot
		address; timer_ctrl and counter contain before/after physical
		timer snapshots. resumes counts returns through cpu_resume.
		cold counts hardware-mode cpu_resume returns, aborts counts WFI
		returns without reset, and errata counts completed sibling-core
		L2 recovery sequences. L2 control/cache reset policy and temporary
		watchdog before/armed/restored values are also captured.
		sleep_clock ready records the ARM persistent-clock provider; ticks
		and counter record paired PCM 32.768 kHz and physical CNT samples.
		stopped_ns is the nonnegative PCM interval minus CNT time when
		F26M is handed off. It is added before timekeeping resumes.
		Generic timekeeping uses the composite clock instead of injecting
		second-granularity RTC sleep time a second time.
		entry state is the last platform suspend_state_t (standby=2,
		mem=3); cpu0_mode is the effective entry mode, distinct from the
		qualification cpu0 mode setting printed below. fallback records an
		automatic deep request retried with retention after a pre-entry
		-EBUSY and successful rollback; deep_requests/deep_fallbacks count
		these requests/fallbacks. fallback source/r0/infra retain blocker
		masks from that rejected attempt. Actual resume failures never
		trigger a fallback and are reported normally.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/cpu0_mode
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		CPU0 entry mode for explicit standby: 0 (default) retains normal
		WFI, 1 saves ARM/CPU-PM context, waits for wakeup, then performs
		a software MMU-off restart through cpu_resume before restoring
		the original shared boot vector and PM state. Mode 1 keeps CPU0,
		L2, infra, DDR and supplies powered; it qualifies the resume entry
		and does not prove hardware power-down or Boot ROM handoff.
		Mode 2 permits PCM CPU0/TOP/L2 power-down, exits cache coherency,
		and uses the hardware reset vector; L2, banked and notifier state
		are restored, including the BSP sibling-core erratum sequence.
		It requires the UART/domain/source handoff checks to pass and
		retains infra/DDRPHY/crystal control unless their separate controls
		below are enabled; supply voltage policy is unchanged.
		Mode 1 temporarily arms a 30-second hardware reset watchdog
		after normal device suspend, restoring its settings on return.
		A stopped watchdog may retain its IRQ/dual-mode selection: the
		guard clears that selection temporarily and restores it unchanged.
		An enabled IRQ/dual-mode watchdog is rejected with -EBUSY.
		PCM timer values above 20 seconds are rejected in mode 1; with
		timer=0 an external wake must arrive before its watchdog.
		Mode 2 requires the normal watchdog device suspend to have
		stopped the hardware watchdog. It neither arms a temporary guard
		nor writes watchdog registers, allowing long hardware sleep.
		An enabled watchdog rejects mode 2 before CPU power-down.
		Android's default s2idle is unchanged. Values above 2 are rejected.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/pcm_timer_ms
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Optional PCM timer for explicit standby, in milliseconds, 0..60000.
		Default 0 selects external wakeup. With the platform sleep clock
		available, its timer still counts to U32_MAX (about 36.4 hours) so
		external wake intervals can be measured; rollover also wakes PCM.
		Without that clock, 0 disables the timer. A nonzero value arms a
		32.768 kHz PCM timer for the next standby entry. It neither
		changes Android's default s2idle policy nor enables power gating.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/r0_control
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Boolean, default false. Qualify the PCM R0 power-control connection
		during explicit CPU0-reset standby (cpu0_mode=2). Requires UART/USB
		clock handoff, qualified firmware baseline, MD1/CONN/DISP/MFG/ISP
		domains off and external/MD1/CONN clock requests clear. F26M is forced
		unless f26m_control is enabled; APSRC is forced unless apsrc_control
		is enabled. R0 alone does not permit crystal stop or DDR power changes.
		R0 must return to POWER_ON_VAL0 before disconnecting PCM output.
		The BSP SYSCLK settle selector and 99-tick (about 3 ms) budget are
		prepared only for this qualification. Readback includes the MD
		contribution; unsigned differences compensate it for programming
		and restoration. The original total and selector are restored on exit.
		State adds sysclk_settle before/md/programmed/applied/wake/restored.
		With F26M forced, this checks programming and restoration only;
		physical oscillator restart timing remains unqualified.
		State adds r0 requested/value/baseline/blockers. Blocker bits are
		wrong CPU mode (0), ordinary source handoff failure (1), powered
		non-CPU domain (2), or hardware source-clock request (3).

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/apsrc_control
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Boolean, default false. Release the APSRC software override during
		explicit standby with cpu0_mode=2 and r0_control=1. All R0 guards
		apply. Requires a bound DDR supplier and the four MT6580 BSP
		DDRPHY SPM prerequisite fields to match before entry and on resume.
		Offset 0x5cc bit 31 may be clear or set as in the BSP PCM APSRC
		routines; all other bits must match. Snapshots retain the complete value.
		F26M is retained unless f26m_control is also enabled. DDRPHY/infra
		power, voltage and memory PLL policy are retained.
		This hands APSRC to hardware without proving DDR self-refresh duration.
		State adds apsrc requested/ddr_check and DDRPHY before/after snapshots
		for offsets 0x5c0, 0x5c4, 0x5c8 and 0x5cc. Failed prerequisites abort
		before connecting outputs; all control registers are restored on exit.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/f26m_control
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Boolean, default false. Hand F26M to hardware during explicit standby.
		Requires cpu0_mode=2, r0_control=1, apsrc_control=1 and all their UART,
		USB, power-domain, firmware and DDR prerequisite checks. CCIF masks
		are preserved. Uses the MT6580 BSP CLK_CON SRCLKENA mask and MD1
		CXO32K selection with MD1 off, plus the qualified SYSCLK settle budget.
		CLK_CON expected/wake/restored snapshots verify setup and rollback.
		CPU/L2 may reset; infra/DDRPHY stay retained unless separately
		enabled below. Voltage policy stays retained.
		Physical counter/RTC snapshots are needed to qualify actual clock stop;
		successful register handoff alone does not prove crystal shutdown.
		Hardware mode 2 requires the normal watchdog to be stopped; it
		has no temporary reset guard. Android's default s2idle is unchanged.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/ddrphy_control
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Boolean, default false. Allow the BSP PCM DDRPHY power-down sequence
		by clearing DDRPHY_PDN_DIS during explicit CPU0-reset standby.
		Requires cpu0_mode=2, r0_control=1, apsrc_control=1, their dependency
		checks and DPY_PWR_CON=0x0d before entry. f26m_control can be left
		off to qualify PHY power sequencing with 26 MHz retained first.
		Full DDRPHY fixed-field checks and DPY power-control restoration are
		verified on return. State adds ddrphy requested and power before/after.
		Infra power is retained unless infra_control is enabled. Voltage
		and MAINPLL policy remain retained. Hardware mode 2 uses the normal
		watchdog suspend policy without a temporary reset guard.
		Off/on snapshots alone do not measure the time spent powered down.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/infra_control
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Boolean, default false. Allow the BSP PCM infra-power-down branch
		by clearing INFRA_PDN_DIS. Requires all CPU0/R0/APSRC/F26M/DDRPHY
		qualification controls and their existing checks. Additional guards
		require saved native UART context, a prepared seven-word MT6580
		SYSIRQ snapshot, active CIRQ v1 covering SPI32..157, prepared PWRAP
		commands with WACS2 initialized/idle, and powered-on IFR control bits.
		infra requested/blockers/power/sram snapshots retain entry/result.
		Blockers: missing controls (0), IFR baseline (1), UART context (2),
		SYSIRQ context (3), CIRQ (4), PWRAP (5). Failure aborts before output
		handoff. On return the generic power status and IFR on-state must
		match. Voltage and MAINPLL policy stay retained. Hardware mode 2
		uses the normal watchdog suspend policy; Android s2idle is unchanged.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/1000f000.pmic-wrap/spm_phase
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only snapshot of the MT6350 suspend command-slot handoff.
		active indicates an installed suspend table. prepared counts
		successful installations; restored counts successful restores,
		including rollback. saved and staged retain the latest four
		words in ADR4/WDATA4/ADR5/WDATA5 order. They are snapshots, not
		live reads. Staging slots does not execute a PMIC command or
		change voltage; no write operation is provided.
		auxadc contains STRUP_CON10 saved/resume/restored snapshots. After
		PCM execution, only its START bit is restored before releasing the
		slots; unrelated PMIC bits are retained.

What:		/sys/power/mem_sleep (MT6580 deep)
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		The MT6580 PCM provider exposes the standard deep selection.
		With deep selected, mem requests the verified CPU0/L2/infra/DDRPHY
		power-down and APSRC/F26M handoff profile, using the external-wake
		PCM counter and normal watchdog suspend policy. Standby sysfs
		qualification controls/timer are ignored and left unchanged.
		If a supplier/prerequisite rejects entry with -EBUSY before WFI,
		and PCM rollback succeeds, automatic mem uses the retained-power
		profile for that attempt. It never retries a real resume error.
		A1260 initially used mem_sleep_default=s2idle during qualification.
		After physical insertion wake across CPU0/infra/DDRPHY power-down
		and clock stop passed, the device selects mem_sleep_default=deep.
		Deep also parks AXI at 26 MHz and power-cycles MAINPLL using the
		verified software sequence before/after PCM execution. Missing PLL
		suppliers reject entry with -EBUSY before changes, allowing retained
		fallback. Boards opting into mediatek,vproc-retention borrow the
		qualified MT6350 hardware sleep policy during mem; other boards
		retain their prior voltage-bank policy.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/axi_26m_control
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Boolean, default false, applying only to explicit standby qualification.
		Requires cpu0_mode=2, r0_control=1 and their UART/domain/source guards.
		TOPCKGEN and APMIXED suppliers must be bound through the optional
		mediatek,clock-controllers phandles. CPU must use ARMPLL, AXI must
		use the board's MAINPLL_D12 selection, and MAINPLL must be enabled,
		unisolated and powered with its reset released.
		Immediately before PCM_KICK, the single-CPU/IRQs-off finisher switches
		AXI[7:4] from 4 (MAINPLL_D12) to 1 (26 MHz). Selection zero is not
		used. After PCM_RETURN, AXI is restored before sibling-core/L2 recovery.
		The helper preserves all other mux bits and PLL configuration/power.
		Cached state adds axi26 requested/prepared/parked/counts/error,
		AXI before/parked/wake/restored and CPU mux snapshots, plus MAINPLL
		CON0/1/2/3 and PWR_CON0 before/after. PWR_CON0 is offset 0x130.
		Automatic mem/deep ignores this qualification switch and uses AXI
		parking with the MAINPLL transaction below. AXI parking alone does
		not change PLL power; mainpll_control selects it for explicit standby.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/mainpll_control
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Boolean, default false, applying only to explicit standby qualification.
		Requires axi_26m_control=1 and all its CPU0/R0/supplier guards. The
		finisher first parks AXI at 26 MHz, then follows the BSP MAINPLL
		reset/enable/isolation/power-off sequence. On PCM_RETURN it powers
		the PLL back on, waits the BSP 1/1/20 us intervals and verifies the
		original configuration before reconnecting AXI and recovering L2.
		PCW/posdiv, AP_PLL selectors, divider enables and memory PLLs are
		never programmed. Unknown power bits are preserved in each RMW;
		only owned power bits are checked while off, with full baseline
		comparison after recovery. CON1[31] is a PCW trigger and is excluded
		from configuration comparison. An incomplete recovery keeps AXI
		at 26 MHz with ownership/error retained. If PLL power recovery is
		still incomplete after abort cleanup, the driver panics before
		normal device resume rather than running consumers with no clock.
		State adds MAINPLL requested/off, verified power_downs/power_ups,
		off/wake register snapshots and automatic/software_enable recovery
		flags. Automatic means the original powered-on state was already
		present before any software enable; power_ups includes that case.
		Automatic mem/deep ignores this control and enables the transaction
		on every successful deep entry. Retained fallback keeps MAINPLL on.
		Register readback and resumed frequency do not measure sleep current.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/1000f000.pmic-wrap/sleep_voltage
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only VPROC snapshots at platform prepare_late and finish,
		after CPUFreq suspend and before CPUFreq resume, respectively.
		Errors are retained separately for each snapshot; a failed optional
		observation does not alter the established AUXADC/slot handoff.
		Registers in order are 0x216 control, 0x21e software selector,
		0x220 on selector, 0x222 sleep selector, 0x224 actual selector and
		0x230 sleep/transition control. Selector low 7 bits encode
		700000 + value * 6250 microvolts. No voltage/bank write is provided.
		The before/resume values do not sample the rail while CPU is off
		and must not be presented as a measurement of retention voltage.

What:		/sys/devices/platform/10006000.power-controller/*suspend/voltage_bank_control
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Unsigned qualification mode, default 0, affecting explicit standby.
		1 tests software/hardware ON bank ownership with a 1.15625 V marker;
		2 stages the MT6580 BSP's 0.85 V sleep selector, sleep reference,
		soft-change/transition enable and SRCLKEN/oscillator hardware clock
		handoff. Both require CPU0 mode 2 and all R0/APSRC/F26M/DDRPHY/infra/
		AXI/MAINPLL qualification controls. CPUFreq must already have selected
		the 1.15 V suspend OPP; software/on/sleep baseline selectors must all
		be 0x48 with software ownership and sleep transition disabled.
		Mode 2 additionally requires the known software-enabled clock baseline.
		Every added field is checked by readback; an error unwinds through
		platform finish. Return to the software bank and the original actual
		selector is checked before CPUFreq/device resume. Failed bank recovery
		panics rather than resuming a governor with the wrong voltage owner.
		Mode 1 never enables analog-sleep controls. Mode 2 uses the exact
		MT6580 BSP fields; it does not clear unused PCM voltage flags.
		The sleep_voltage snapshot adds bank ownership/counts/error, armed/
		marker/released/restored snapshots and mode-2 clock/reference/slew/
		transition snapshots. resume_error reports observation failure;
		counts include a prepared transaction rolled back after an early abort.
		Automatic mem ignores this qualification control. With board property
		mediatek,vproc-retention it applies mode 2 independently, skipping an
		unsupported/firmware-owned baseline only before any new bank write.
		Retained-power fallback holds F26M and does not request hardware sleep,
		although the prepared bank policy is still restored on return.
		The 0.85 V value is a programmed sleep target, not a rail measurement
		made while the CPU is powered off. Awake OPP limits are unchanged.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../mcusys_state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only MT6580 APMIXEDSYS MCUSYS/BIU DCM diagnostics. owned
		indicates opt-in ownership; valid requires MCUCFG+0x5c bit9 and
		BIU+0 bit12 enabled, with MCUCFG+0x60[4:0]=0x12. before/current
		contain those three raw words in that order; unowned live bits
		can change and are not constant configuration expectations.

		applies counts initialization and late resume repairs;
		resume_fixes counts the latter separately. dvfs pauses/restores/
		failures count CPU frequency handovers. degraded means a failed
		post-clock gate restoration latched the optional policy off after
		checking full-clock operation; the actual new CPU rate remains
		committed. This preserves OPP frequency/voltage accounting.
		SPM state additionally
		reports mcusys active/paused/pauses/restores and before/after
		snapshots for the early AXI/PLL transaction; it includes partial
		pause ownership before the first register write. Runtime
		idle_state blocked clocks counts policy admission failures. Its
		separate clocks active/paused/pauses/restores and before/after
		snapshots report the runtime pause before CPU PM and restore in
		the PCM wait callback before arch/GIC clients exit CPU PM;
		outer cleanup also covers early-WFI or notifier aborts. Counters wrap at32
		bits. Reading the attribute changes no policy or divider.
